xnu: the lab's T8103 bring-up kernel on upstream's own T8103 configuration

The tip counterpart of the kernel half of ../candidate.patch plus ../../m1-display/console-resume.patch
(the working-tree changes of sources/puredarwin-m1-desktop, which is the source every pin
collection's kernel is built from). Base: SiliconForest c713d8fb (upstream-xnu-12377, 11 Nov 2026).

Upstream added a T8103 machine configuration on 10 Nov (fda0135e) for darwin-vm's QEMU machine:
EL2/VHE entry, no AppleARMSMP, SILICONFOREST_NO_KERNEL_INTEGRITY, an embedded-style MASTER file.
What this patch does with each overlapping piece:

  taken from upstream, ours dropped
    MakeInc.def.in   T8103 in SUPPORTED_ARM64_MACHINE_CONFIGS and in the large-memory layout list
    board_config.h   the assembler names HID4, EHID4, CPU_OVRD, CPU_CFG, ACC_OVRD and
                     ARM64_REG_HID4_DisDcMVAOps (upstream: apple_arm64_regs.h, same encodings)
    start.s          upstream's EL2 entry stays; under the m1n1 hypervisor the kernel enters at EL1
                     and the branch is not taken
  ours kept, upstream's replaced or fenced
    MakeInc.def.in   MACHINE_FLAGS_ARM64_T8103: DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP instead of
                     SILICONFOREST_NO_KERNEL_INTEGRITY, which would switch AppleARMSMP off; the lab starts
                     its cores through AppleARMSMP and SFAppleBootCPUPMGR
    MASTER.arm64.t8103  the lab's file (derived from MASTER.arm64.MacOSX) replaces upstream's
                     (xsmall/embedded base, no SysV IPC, pgtrace): a different kernel for user space
    caches_asm.s     upstream's enable_dc_mva_ops, disable_dc_mva_ops and
                     CleanPoC_DcacheRegion_Force_nopreempt[_nohid] are compiled out under
                     DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP in favour of m1_cache_helpers.inc: ours restores the HID4
                     value it found (upstream's clears the enable inside a caller's batch), masks
                     DAIF while the per-core value is live, and returns on an empty range
    board_config.h   KERNEL_INTEGRITY_CTRR undefined and PMAP_CS/XNU_MONITOR left out under
                     DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP (upstream does both through SILICONFOREST_NO_KERNEL_INTEGRITY)
  ours, no upstream counterpart
    CMakeLists.txt (DEBUG only; ../../m1-dcp/kernel-patches/0004 lifts it), sys_recount.c, recount.c,
    arm_init.c, arm_vm_init.c, m1_progress_entry.inc, video_console.c, pe_init.c

diff --git a/src/Kernel/xnu/CMakeLists.txt b/src/Kernel/xnu/CMakeLists.txt
index 04961d66..d10b12c2 100644
--- a/src/Kernel/xnu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/Kernel/xnu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -147,6 +147,12 @@ if(NOT SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG MATCHES "^(RELEASE|DEVELOPMENT|DEBUG|KASAN)$
         "Unsupported SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG='${SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG}'")
 endif()
 
+# The public non-PPL M1 development configuration is deliberately DEBUG-only.
+if(SILICONFOREST_ARM64_MACHINE_CONFIG STREQUAL "T8103" AND
+   NOT SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG STREQUAL "DEBUG")
+    message(FATAL_ERROR "T8103 bringup requires DEBUG")
+endif()
+
 file(MAKE_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/xnu_header_install)
 # a prebuilt header install goes where the in-tree one would, so kexts see the same paths
 set(SILICONFOREST_PREBUILT_XNU_HEADERS "" CACHE PATH "Prebuilt xnu header install to use instead of building it")
